# THE LYING CONTROLS of variable-of-a-loop-is-judged-as-it-is-written-from-source.ir: the test of the loop leaves no room for the step, and EACH IS REPORTED, WHOEVER CALLS
# f1 .. f4 are called once, with 1: the walk knows `to` and with it the variable: UNTIL 0-int32-promises-3 NONE OF THE FOUR WAS REPORTED. f5 .. f8 are the same four, and nobody knows who calls them
# inclusive: `i <= to` lets 2147483647 in . byTwo: room for one is not room for two . testedAfter: the step comes in front of the test . reassigned: what is stored in the body has passed no test
# f9 .. f16: where the climb for relations may not find one: f9 afterTheLoop: the loop is left with the limit reached . f10 siblingArm, f14 testInOneArm: the test stands in an arm that the step is not below . f11 testBehindTheStep
# f12 stepWithoutTest: a way leads round the test . f13 testOfTheOldValue: the variable was stored into since . f15 otherVariable . f16 widerLimit: below a number is not below an int32
